course: dictionary
lesson: 239
title: Mixing metals to make alloys
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An alloy is a metal made by mixing two or more metals, or a metal with another element. Mixing them makes the new metal stronger or better than the pure metal alone. To alloy means to mix metals together like this.
explain: «Bronze is an alloy of copper and tin; it is harder than either metal.» Bronze is made from two metals. It is harder than copper, and harder than tin too. Mixing can give a better result than either metal on its own.
explain: «Mixing metals makes alloys that are better than the pure metals.» Steel is iron with a little carbon, and it is strong enough for bridges. Alloy wheels on a car are made of a light metal alloy, so an alloy can be both strong and light.
fact: An alloy is a metal made by mixing two or more metals, or a metal with another element.
fact: «Bronze» is an alloy of copper and tin.
fact: «Steel» is iron with a little carbon, and it is strong enough for bridges.
fact: «Brass» is an alloy of copper and zinc, and it is used in coins and musical instruments.
fact: The Bronze Age began over 5000 years ago.
exercise: «Bronze is an alloy of copper and tin.» What is bronze made from? | Gold and silver | Iron and carbon | Copper and zinc | *Copper and tin
exercise: «Steel» is iron with a little carbon. Why is steel used for bridges? | *It is strong enough to hold heavy loads | It is clear like glass | It is light enough to float | It is soft enough to bend easily
exercise: Which word is the name for a metal made by mixing two or more metals? | Wire | Ore | *Alloy | Foil
test: Why are alloys often better than pure metals? | Alloys never break, whatever happens | Mixing metals makes them always lighter than air | Alloys are made from only one metal | *Mixing metals makes them stronger or better
test: Alloy wheels on a car are made of what? | Plastic | Wood | Pure gold | *A light metal alloy
exam: Which alloy is made from copper and zinc? | Steel | Bronze | Iron | *Brass
